Licence of the weights
  Meta gives no separate licence and no model card for the pretrained
  weights. The only licence statement covers the whole project:
  README.md, section "License" (lines 300-302 at the pinned commit):
  "Demucs is released under the MIT license as found in the LICENSE
  file." setup.py also says license='MIT License', and the MIT-licensed
  code names the weight URLs (demucs/remote/files.txt, demucs/pretrained.py
  ROOT_URL). We host the official files unchanged under that statement,
  with the MIT text next to them. This is a project-wide line, not a
  licence written for the weights.

  The models were trained on MUSDB18-HQ and an extra set of 800 songs
  (README.md line 30 and line 222). That training data has its own terms.
  We do not host or give out any of it.

Port of the Demucs processing (MIT, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc.
and affiliates)
  The page does the steps around the network core in JS. They follow the
  Demucs code:
    engine/dsp.js      demucs/spec.py spectro and ispectro (torch.stft and
                       torch.istft), demucs/htdemucs.py HTDemucs._spec,
                       _magnitude, _mask (cac) and _ispec, and the track
                       normalisation of demucs/api.py separate_tensor
    engine/segment.js  demucs/apply.py apply_model (the shifts and split
                       branches, the transition weight), TensorChunk.padded
                       and demucs/utils.py center_trim
  The model tools in tools/stem-splitter/ (core.py, export.py,
  demucs_np.py, thzip.py) follow the same files and HTDemucs.forward.

Test audio
  The tests use only synth-v1, a synthetic signal made for this site
  (CONTRACT.md 3.5; tools/stem-splitter/synth.py, engine/synth.js). No
  music with copyright is in this folder or in the tests.

